  "market_context": "EUR/USD was in a higher-time-frame uptrend on the 4H chart; price approached a major structure level (0.98200) from above, forming a short-term downtrend on the 1H chart ahead of the reversal setup.",
  "key_observation": "A major level of structure at 0.98200—previously acting as both support and resistance—was tested twice on the 1H chart, forming a double bottom pattern confirmed by a bullish engulfing candle, signaling short-term trend reversal.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: On the 4H EUR/USD chart, the analyst identified a major level of structure at 0.98200 that had recently served as both support and resistance multiple times during the ongoing uptrend.",
    "Step 2: The analyst noted the market was approaching this level from above, indicating a short-term downtrend on lower time frames, and expected rejection at this demand zone.",
    "Step 3: Zooming into the 1H chart, the analyst observed price testing the 0.98200 zone twice, forming a double bottom pattern where the second low failed to break below the first.",
    "Step 4: Upon the second test, a bullish engulfing candlestick formed, confirming the reversal signal and triggering the long entry.",
    "Step 5: The stop-loss was placed one ATR below the lowest point of the swing low (the double bottom), and profit was tracked toward the next HTF structure level."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Combining HTF major structure levels with LTF reversal patterns (e.g., double bottom + engulfing) increases trade probability; entries on second test with confirmation candles offer optimal risk-reward for reversals.",
